<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Privacy Policy — MediaHub</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css"></head><body><main class="wrap"><header><img src="/logo.svg" width="48" height="48" alt=""><a href="/" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none">MediaHub</a></header><article class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">LAST UPDATED: OCTOBER 10, 2026</p><h1>Privacy <em>Policy</em></h1><p>This is a non-commercial personal hobby project for connecting a user's MyAnimeList account to MediaHub features.</p><h2>Information processed</h2><p>If you choose to connect MyAnimeList, MediaHub processes the authorization tokens returned by MyAnimeList and basic account information such as your username and ID. When you request your list, it processes anime titles, list statuses, ratings, and related list data returned by the MyAnimeList API.</p><h2>Purpose and storage</h2><p>The information is used only to provide the features you request, such as displaying and analyzing your anime list. OAuth session data is stored in an encrypted, HttpOnly, Secure cookie on your browser. The server is configured not to intentionally log access tokens or refresh tokens. Clearing the session cookie or choosing Disconnect removes the local session.</p><h2>Third parties</h2><p>Authentication and anime-list data are provided by MyAnimeList and are subject to its own terms and privacy policy. The app may be hosted by a third-party hosting provider. Do not use this project for sensitive information.</p><h2>Retention and security</h2><p>The project aims to keep only the session data needed to provide the connection. No system can guarantee absolute security. Do not share credentials, and disconnect when you no longer want to use the integration.</p><h2>Your choices</h2><p>You may decline authorization, disconnect at any time, or stop using the service. You can request deletion or clarification by contacting the project owner through the repository where this project is published.</p><p><strong>Contact:</strong> project owner via the linked source repository. Before public launch, replace this with a working contact method and confirm the policy matches the final deployment.</p><p><a href="/">Return to MediaHub</a></p></article><footer><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a><a href="/terms">Terms</a></footer></main></body></html>
